{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed402918419/6/prompt.md')\ntext = p.read_text()\nprint(text[:4000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"7b0280bc\" lines=\"54-69\">\n<description>\nRecolor the shortest path between two terminal squares in a square-and-track graph.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Two non-bg colors form solid NxN squares (N>=2): one color marks exactly 2 terminals, the other marks stations.\n- A third non-bg color forms 1-cell-wide track segments connecting pairs of squares (graph edges).\n\nRule:\n- Find the shortest path (fewest edges) between the two terminal squares.\n- Recolor every station square on that path to green.\n- Recolor every track segment along that path to grey.\n- Everything else unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The grid encodes a graph where squares are nodes and tracks are edges; the task is graph shortest-path, not spatial proximity.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"28a6681f\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\nSimulate water pixels falling under gravity into basins formed by colored obstacles.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 0. Water pixels = color 1 (blue).\n- Other colors form static solid structures (walls, steps, containers).\n- Water starts in unstable positions above or beside basins.\n\nRule:\n- Each water pixel falls straight down through bg cells.\n- When blocked below, it slides diagonally through the unique open side cell.\n- When resting on a surface, it slides horizontally toward the nearest gap where it can fall again.\n- Process repeats until no water pixel moves.\n\nKey insight: Water seeks the deepest reachable basin via diagonal and horizontal sliding, not just vertical fall.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\" lines=\"42-56\">\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9b30e358\" lines=\"9-23\">\n<description>\nRepeat the bottom foreground motif upward until it fills the whole grid.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The only foreground pixels occupy a contiguous block of rows at the bottom.\n- That bottom block is the complete vertical motif, including its background cells.\n\nRule\n- Copy the bottom motif rows repeatedly upward across the full grid.\n- Preserve horizontal alignment and vertical phase: the original first motif row remains at its input row.\n- The output shape is unchanged.\n\nKey insight\nThe blank rows above the bottom foreground block are missing repetitions of the same row motif, not empty space.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"758abdf0\" lines=\"54-69\">\n<description>\nAdvance short marker bars away from the full edge bar, turning completed two-pixel markers into edge-color marks at the opposite side.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One non-background color forms a complete one-cell-thick bar on exactly one outer edge.\n- The other foreground color appears only in the first two cells inward from that bar, lane by lane.\n\nRule\n- In each lane perpendicular to the edge bar, a one-pixel marker adjacent to the bar grows one more cell inward.\n- A two-pixel marker in those first two inward cells is cleared\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
